  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You're given a sorted array of unique integers `nums`.\n\n**Return the smallest sorted list of ranges that exactly covers every number in `nums`, where each range is represented as [start, end].**\n\nIf a range covers only a single number, still represent it as [start, start].",
    "constraints": [
      "0 <= nums.length <= 25",
      "-2^31 <= nums[i] <= 2^31 - 1",
      "all values in nums are unique",
      "nums is sorted in strictly increasing order"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Single line: JSON array of all arguments, e.g. [arg1, arg2, ...]",
    "outputFormat": "Single line: JSON-serialised return value",
    "sampleTestCases": [
